  "notes": "USAGE:\nA formal word used in news, legal, and academic contexts. In grammar studies, {伝聞|でんぶん} also refers to the hearsay evidential form (〜そうだ, 〜とのことだ) — a way of marking that information comes from a secondary source.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {伝聞|でんぶん}によると (according to what one has heard)\n- {伝聞|でんぶん}{情報|じょうほう} (hearsay information)\n- {伝聞|でんぶん}{証拠|しょうこ} (hearsay evidence)\n- {伝聞|でんぶん}にすぎない (nothing more than hearsay)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- うわさ: rumor — more colloquial and informal\n- {風聞|ふうぶん}: rumor — literary synonym, less common\n- {又聞|またぎ}き: secondhand information — specifically means hearing something through an intermediary",
